WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.720
As television has become more serialized over
the years, major character deaths have become

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.140
increasingly commonplace.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.640
Sometimes, however, a death is poorly planned
or executed, and it tends to stand out like

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.400
a sore thumb.

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.520
Here are some of the shows that killed characters
who should have lived.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.320
From the very beginning, Netflix's Orange
is the New Black has had a highly-developed

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.540
sense of social justice and an admirable dedication
to in representation.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.600
With this comedy/drama set in a women's prison,
creator Jenji Kohan and her writers have attempted

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.210
to balance a stark look at criminal justice
in America, with a dash of comedy and a cast

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.420
of likable characters, many of whom are LGBTQ
women and women of color.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.880
One of the most likable characters from day
one was Poussey Washington, a smart and funny

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.840
black woman who ended up in prison for minor
drug charges.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:49.240
Of all the women on the show, she was perhaps
the kindest and the most helpful to her fellow

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:49.740
inmates.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.200
She also had some of the show's most moving
romantic storylines, from her unrequited feelings

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:58.460
for her best friend Taystee to her eventual
relationship with another inmate, Brooke.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.880
"You can't live your life according to maybes."

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:06.680
During the show's run, the Black Lives Matter
movement was gaining steam in the real world,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.840
reacting against the unjust deaths of black
Americans at the hands of law enforcement.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.260
Naturally, a show as keen to promote social
justice as Orange is the New Black wanted

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.120
to reflect that reality in a story.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.800
So in the fourth season, Poussey was accidentally
suffocated by a guard when she attempted to

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.640
diffuse an escalating situation.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.400
Unfortunately, the show went on to attempt
to make the guard who killed her a sympathetic

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:27.900
character.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:32.280
Fans were understandably angry and the show
became that much less lovable for the loss

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.760
of its most likable character.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:39.400
In its first season, Netflix's House of Cards
was a story told from two opposing angles:

00:01:39.409 --> 00:01:43.630
corrupt politician Frank Underwood and young
investigative reporter Zoe Barnes.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:47.590
As Frank plotted and schemed to gain more
and more power, Zoe attempted to uncover the

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.220
truth about him.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.220
Although he manipulated her for a while, and
the two even shared a creepy semi-romantic

00:01:53.229 --> 00:01:56.720
relationship, Zoe was the first to realize
Frank had murdered Congressman Peter Russo

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.860
and wanted to see him brought to justice.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.800
That's where Season 1 ended, and it was reasonable
to assume Season 2 would see her quest continue.

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:07.360
"Underwood's been using you Zoe don’t you
want to know why?"

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.840
Instead, the Season 2 premiere saw Underwood
murder Zoe by pushing her in front of a subway

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.340
train.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.680
From that point on, House of Cards becomes
a story about the bad guys winning, and loses

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.319
all interest in featuring sympathetic protagonists.

00:02:20.319 --> 00:02:24.540
Moreover, Frank's murder of Zoe marks his
turn from an amoral politician who'd once

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.200
killed in a moment of opportunity to a cartoonish
supervillain who could get away with anything.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:33.500
The series maintained its popularity for a
while, but its story never really recovered.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.220
Fifteen years ago, LGBTQ relationships were much less common on television than they are

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.700
today, but Buffy the Vampire Slayer offered
one of TV's earliest examples, in the romance

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:45.940
between Willow Rosenberg and Tara Maclay.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.060
For a couple of years after their meeting
in Season 4, nothing could keep them apart.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:54.180
Their relationship got rocky in Season 6,
but that wasn't too surprising on a show that

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.060
never shied away from a bit of soap opera-style
drama.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.680
What was surprising was the moment later in
the season when, just as Willow and Tara had

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.880
overcome their problems and were recommitting
to their relationship, Tara was hit by a stray

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:08.620
bullet fired by a villain who had come looking
for Buffy.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:12.980
Tara died in Willow's arms, and the rest of
the season became the story of Willow's unhinged

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:17.280
quest for revenge against not just the villain
in question, but the entire world.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:21.800
The loss of Tara wasn't just a blow to the
show and its audience it was also an ignominious

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:25.420
ending to one of television's first great
lesbian relationships.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.720
John Locke died halfway through the fifth
season of Lost, but the actor who played him,

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:32.240
Terry O'Quinn, was a regular on the show until
it ended.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.600
In addition to flashbacks, Locke appeared
in the Purgatory-esque "flash sideways" scenes

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:37.720
during the sixth season.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.180
However, O'Quinn also took on a new role as
the Man in Black, previously known as the

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:46.580
Smoke Monster, who took Locke's shape as his
primary human form after Locke's death.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.720
"John Locke was not a believer Jack.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.380
He was a sucker."

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.720
John Locke, with his unshakeable and sometimes
irrational faith in the power of the island,

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:01.459
could be an aggravating character at times,
but he was set up throughout the series as

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.380
a heroic and hugely important figure.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:08.600
Then, suddenly, he died a pathetic death strangled
with an extension cord in a hotel room and

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.250
his form was used as a host for a force of
evil.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.970
Ultimately, Locke finds peace in the afterlife,
but it was hard to watch that last season

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:16.680
without thinking that he deserved better.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.259
Torchwood, an edgier spin-off of Doctor Who
about an extra-governmental agency that investigates

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:25.500
the supernatural, seemed to really enjoy killing
off its characters.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.300
By the time the third season rolled around,
only three members of Torchwood remained:

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:32.460
Jack Harkness, Gwen Cooper, and Ianto Jones.

00:04:32.469 --> 00:04:36.550
However, the five episodes which made up the
third season, otherwise known as Children

00:04:36.550 --> 00:04:39.879
of Earth, had an even darker tone than the
seasons that had come before.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.180
It was Ianto who paid the ultimate price for
that.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.380
"I love you."

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:48.360
"Don't."

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.880
This upset many viewers, particularly because
Ianto was in a gay relationship with Torchwood

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:55.160
leader Jack Harkness.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.120
Fans accused the series and its creators of
homophobia, despite the fact that showrunner

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.720
Russell T. Davies is himself a gay man as
is John Barrowman, who played Jack.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.360
Nevertheless, Davies had unintentionally stumbled
into the longstanding and unfortunate cultural

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:11.160
trope of killing LGBTQ characters in fiction.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:16.080
Lexa was the character whose death brought
criticism of what's often called the "bury

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:18.280
your gays" trope into mainstream discourse.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.639
Played by Alycia Debnam-Carey on the CW sci-fi
series The 100, Lexa was the leader of a warrior

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.440
tribe on a post-apocalyptic Earth.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.940
Drama ensued when she fell in love with Clarke,
leader of a group of delinquent teenagers

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:33.220
who'd been sent back to the planet by human
refugees in space.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.659
Their political responsibilities complicated
their feelings, but they found each other

00:05:36.659 --> 00:05:39.310
nonetheless and soon began a romantic relationship.

00:05:39.310 --> 00:05:43.360
Unfortunately, Debnam-Carey was also one of
the stars of Fear the Walking Dead, and its

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.860
Season 2 shooting schedule interfered with
The 100.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.960
So just as she had finally found a moment's
happiness with Clarke, Lexa was killed off.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.360
Not only that, but she was also shot by someone
who wasn't even aiming at her exactly like

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:56.559
Tara on Buffy the Vampire Slayer.

00:05:56.559 --> 00:06:01.939
The show's fan base, which included many LGBTQ
viewers, was outraged by this turn of events,

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:04.059
with many vowing never to watch the show again.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.740
It became impossible to discuss The 100 without
talking about the Lexa problem, which cast

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:11.580
a shadow over discourse about the series until
its end.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:16.980
The BBC costume drama Downton Abbey was very
much an ensemble show, but Matthew Crawley

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.360
was a principal protagonist from the very
beginning.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:24.080
He's introduced as a distant cousin of patriarch
Lord Grantham, and becomes the heir to Downton

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:27.060
Abbey when Grantham's previous heirs die on
the Titanic.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:31.800
He serves as an important audience identification
character, adjusting to life on the lavish

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:36.000
estate, and also engages in a doomed romance
with Mary Crawley, Grantham's daughter.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:40.360
The two eventually wed and have a son, but
one day Matthew suddenly dies in an automobile

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:40.860
accident.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:45.319
Unfortunately, there was no way Matthew could
remain on the show, because Dan Stevens wanted

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:49.569
to pursue a movie career and was free to leave
after Season 3's Christmas special.

00:06:49.569 --> 00:06:53.840
However, the romance between Matthew and Mary
had been a fan-favorite aspect on the show,

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:57.779
and his rise to become Lord of Downton Abbey
was a central element of the series from the

00:06:57.780 --> 00:06:58.580
very beginning.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:02.339
Matthew's sudden death so totally derailed
the show's storyline that it might have been

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:04.420
better to just end it when Stevens left.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:09.879
How I Met Your Mother was presented as a story
told by Ted Mosby to his kids, explaining

00:07:09.879 --> 00:07:13.840
how his relationship with their mother began,
and diverging into countless stories of other

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:15.200
relationships along the way.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.979
But the title character, Tracy McConnell,
doesn't really show up until the finale of

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:22.560
Season 8, and doesn't become a regular character
until the ninth season.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:26.580
It took a long time to get there, but Ted
and Tracy's romance actually plays out pretty

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.800
well in the final season.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.420
"Funny how sometimes you just find things."

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:37.860
Despite everything that had happened over
nine years, viewers were primed to watch Ted

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:39.660
and Tracy live happily ever after.

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:43.919
And then things took a turn when it was revealed
that, while Ted has been telling the story

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:46.809
to his kids, their mother has been dead for
six years.

00:07:46.809 --> 00:07:51.210
She passed away from an undisclosed illness,
and Ted has been a single father ever since.

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:55.050
This sets up the reveal that Robin, who Ted
fell in love with in the series premiere,

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:58.389
is the real love of his life and the woman
he was meant to grow old with.

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:02.029
That might have worked better if she hadn't
spent so much of the show romantically involved

00:08:02.029 --> 00:08:06.009
with Ted's friend Barney, who she marries
and divorces during the series finale.

00:08:06.009 --> 00:08:09.919
The show's creators offered the defense that
this had been the plan all along, but after

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:11.820
such a long run it just didn't work.

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:16.409
The twist made Tracy feel like nothing more
than a prop, and left a very bad taste in

00:08:16.409 --> 00:08:17.460
the mouths of viewers.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:22.800
Allison Argent was a hugely important character
during the first three seasons of Teen Wolf.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:26.000
She started out as the love interest of Scott
McCall, the show's lead.

00:08:26.169 --> 00:08:30.300
Their relationship was complicated by the
fact that Allison came from a family of werewolf

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:32.340
hunters, while Scott was a werewolf himself.

00:08:32.529 --> 00:08:36.640
By season 3, however, Scott and Allison's
romantic relationship was over, though they

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.080
remained friends and allies.

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:42.700
More importantly, actress Crystal Reed wanted
to try other things, and felt a bit stifled

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:46.140
as a 29-year-old actress playing a 17-year-old
character.

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:49.910
So she made the decision to leave the series,
and at the end of the season Allison was run

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.000
through with a sword by an Oni demon.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:56.120
It was probably the right decision for Reed,
but Allison was such a strong part of the

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.040
series that Teen Wolf was never quite the
same without her.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.460
Madison Clark was the glue that held Fear
the Walking Dead together for three whole

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.120
seasons.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:08.100
The show began by focusing on her family,
as the high school guidance counselor protected

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:12.320
her son, daughter, husband, and stepson from
an escalating zombie apocalypse.

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:17.220
It was a great role for Kim Dickens, a talented
actress who rarely had a better chance to

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:21.190
shine, and putting a capable middle-aged woman
in the lead made Fear stand out from most

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:25.260
of the rugged-man-dominated zombie genre,
including the show it had spun off from.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:29.740
Nevertheless, after teasing her absence for
the first few episodes of season 4, the show

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:34.310
revealed in a flashback that Madison had sacrificed
her life by leading a horde of zombies to

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.300
their doom while the other humans escaped.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:39.760
When something like that happens to a lead
character, you might assume it's because the

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.820
actor wanted out.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:45.210
This time, however, Kim Dickens was as surprised
as anyone to find out her character was dying,

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.660
and described herself as heartbroken about
the news.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.010
New showrunners Ian Goldberg and Andrew Chambliss
claimed they wanted to kill Madison as part

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.820
of their vision for the show, but it still
seems like a strange decision to make.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:59.680
Madison was what made Fear the Walking Dead
different from all the other zombie stories

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:00.180
out there.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.500
So why get rid of her and become more of the
same?

